  "reason": "The current best (config_009, acc=0.6352) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted. The evidence strongly supports this architectural backbone: multiprofile >> singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat. The main untested dimension in this optimal setup is the RNA encoder. scgpt performed poorly in singleprofile (0.4275 vs 0.5266 for pca), but scvi_n200 is entirely untested and uses a fundamentally different (variational) representation that may capture complementary biological signal. Config_032 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted) isolates this one variable while preserving all proven-optimal settings. With only 3 experiments remaining, this is the highest-value test: if scvi_n200 matches or beats pca, we identify a new direction; if not, we confirm pca_n2000 is optimal and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning other aspects."
